<p>Music enthusiasts rejoice: the organizers of the <strong>Horizon Summer Music Festival</strong> have officially dropped their most eclectic and ambitious artist roster to date. Spanning three days and six stages across scenic lakeside parklands, this year's edition promises unprecedented acoustic production and stellar genre crossovers.</p>

<p>Headlining Friday night is synth-pop titan <em>The Midnight Echo</em>, followed by Saturday's double-bill featuring hip-hop visionary <em>K-Lyric</em> and electronic duo <em>Solstice</em>. Sunday culminates in an orchestral sunset performance led by ambient composer <em>Aurora</em>.</p>

<h2>Stage Highlights & Sound Innovation</h2>
<p>Beyond the marquee names, the 2026 festival introduces two newly designed acoustic domes powered by 360-degree object-based spatial audio:</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>The Meadow Mainstage:</strong> Houses the massive LED holographic canopy and high-output line array system designed for headline rock and electronic sets.</li>
    <li><strong>The Forest Acoustic Shell:</strong> An intimate natural amphitheater constructed from reclaimed cedar, tailored for unplugged acoustic sessions and spoken word.</li>
    <li><strong>The Resonance Sphere:</strong> An experimental binaural dome where attendees receive custom high-fidelity wireless headsets for immersive ambient listening sessions.</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>
    "Our goal was not just to book big names, but to curate an auditory journey where festivalgoers discover their next favorite indie band in breathtaking outdoor settings."
    <br><br><strong>— Claire Vance, Festival Creative Director</strong>
</blockquote>

<h2>Tickets, Camping & Eco-Initiatives</h2>
<p>In accordance with regional sustainability mandates, the festival operates on a strict zero-single-use-plastic policy. All food vendors utilize 100% compostable packaging, and camping zones feature solar-powered charging pods and greywater filtration systems.</p>

<p>Early bird three-day passes go on sale this Friday, with tiered single-day admission following next Monday. Given previous years' instant sellouts, prospective attendees are encouraged to register their digital queues in advance.</p>

